          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A tankless water heater costs $1,500 to $6,500 installed for most homes, and the unit is the smallest and least variable part of that number. Gas line size, venting route and electrical capacity decide where you land, so get itemised installed quotes before you fall for a model.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            On energy alone, tankless rarely pays back fast. On lifespan, convenience and space, it can be a fair deal for a household staying put with the right gas supply. If you heat with electricity and want the lowest bills, look at a heat pump unit first; if tankless fits your house, our tested picks will get you the right one.
